---
import Section from "../../components/Section.astro";
import ProjectLayout from "../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro";
import Flutter from "../../components/icons/Flutter.astro";
import Figma from "../../components/icons/Figma.astro";

const project = {
    name: "Cookster",
    description: "Figma designs for a mobile catering platform."
}
---

<ProjectLayout description={project.description} title={project.name}>
    <Section slot="show-section">
        <img class="mx-auto" src="/img/cubes/cookster.webp" />
    </Section>

    <Section slot="tell-section">
        <div class="p-10">
            <p>
                At first my goal was mainly getting more experience with mobile app design and development technology.
            <p>
            <br>
                I planned out the first few interfaces using Figma and put them into action with Flutter.
            <p>
            <br>
                After getting familiar with Pocketbase, I implemented basic authentication, a profile page as well as fundamental database presets for later use.
            </p>
        </div>
    </Section>

    <Section slot="detail-section">
        <div class="flex flex-col h-full p-10">
            <p>
                Cookster is supposed to function as a “Catering as a service” application with users signing up for free while caterers have to pay a monthly fee depending on their plan.
            <p>
            <br>
                The main reason for choosing Pocketbase as a backend was primarily to be able to create a working prototype as fast as possible.
            </p>

            <hr class="my-10">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-2xl">Technologies</h3>
            <br>
            <div class="flex gap-10">
                <Flutter />
                <Figma />
            </div>
        </div>
    </Section>
</ProjectLayout>